From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: no auto-hibern8 on Eliza

On the Retroid Pocket Duo (Eliza) a read issued a few seconds after
boot sometimes never completes (2 of 5 boots): the host has entered
hibern8 on its own (HW_H8_ENTER_CNT=1, HW_H8_EXIT_CNT=0), clock gating
then enters hibern8 again from software on top of it
(SW_AFTER_HW_H8_ENTER_CNT=1), and after the software exit the link
never serves the request. The SCSI timeout fires at 30 s, the abort,
device reset and link startup all fail and UFS is gone for that boot.

Leave hibern8 to clock gating alone on Eliza: mark auto-hibern8 broken,
which also skips the hardware clock control that goes with it. Other
SoCs keep the SM8550 data unchanged.


---
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -3030,6 +3030,18 @@
 	.no_phy_retention = true,
 };

+/*
+ * Eliza (Retroid Pocket Duo): with auto-hibern8 on, a request issued after
+ * the hardware entered hibern8 and clock gating entered it again from
+ * software sometimes never completes, and UFS is lost after the 30 s SCSI
+ * timeout. Clock gating still puts the link in hibern8 when idle.
+ */
+static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_eliza_drvdata = {
+	.quirks = UFSHCD_QUIRK_BROKEN_LSDBS_CAP |
+		  UFSHCD_QUIRK_BROKEN_AUTO_HIBERN8,
+	.no_phy_retention = true,
+};
+
 static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_sa8255p_drvdata = {
 	.vops = &ufs_hba_qcom_sa8255p_vops
 };
@@ -3038,7 +3050,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,ufshc" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
-	{ .compatible = "qcom,eliza-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,eliza-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_eliza_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sa8255p-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sa8255p_drvdata },
 	{},
 };
